# Every text file is LF in the working tree on every platform, not just in the repository.
# Without `eol=lf`, a machine with `core.autocrlf=true` gets CRLF on checkout, and
# `prettier --check .` fails on a fresh clone because Prettier's `endOfLine` default is `lf`.
# Setting `endOfLine` to `auto` or `crlf` instead would make the result depend on the machine,
# and GitHub Actions runs Linux while development here happens on Windows.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Generated by `bun install`. Text, but never hand-edited, so keep it out of diffs and out of the
# language statistics.
bun.lock text eol=lf -diff linguist-generated

# Raster images and icons. Declared so the `text=auto` heuristic can never guess wrong and corrupt
# one by rewriting bytes that happen to look like line endings.
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.jpeg binary
*.webp binary
*.avif binary
*.ico binary

# Web fonts, for the same reason.
*.woff binary
*.woff2 binary
*.ttf binary
*.otf binary

# SVG is XML, so it stays text and follows the LF rule above.
*.svg text eol=lf
